  "rules": [
    "Apply a downward correction factor of approximately 10-15% to the model's 30-day forecast average when recent history shows a sharp spike (e.g., >88) followed by volatility, as models consistently overshoot the subsequent mean-reversion phase.",
    "Reduce forecasted growth rates significantly if sentiment history contains isolated positive spikes (0.20-0.50) amidst otherwise neutral (0.00) periods; these sentiment signals often precede short-term rallies that fail to sustain into the 30-day horizon.",
    "Expect high volatility and range-bound outcomes rather than directional trends in the forecast window when recent history exhibits a 'spike-and-drop' pattern, indicating mean reversion will dominate the model's linear projection.",
    "Adjust forecasts downward by roughly 5-8 EUR per day if the last 3 days of history show a decline from a peak while sentiment remains neutral or slightly positive, signaling that momentum is exhausted despite favorable market mood."
  ]
}
